4 balance = balance + 1;

5 Pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);

You might also notice here that the POSIX version passes a variable to lock and unlock, as we may be using different locks to protect different variables. Doing so can increase concurrency: instead of one big lock that is used any time any critical section is accessed (a coarse-grained locking strategy), one will often protect different data and data structures with different locks, thus allowing more threads to be in locked code at once (a more ﬁne-grained approach).

